<title>POLAND: Polish wheat prices slip last week, rye rise.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat prices slip last week, rye rise.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wheat prices slipped during last week's grain auctions, while rye rose and barley held flat, the Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>	   POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>   Product   week to Feb 8     previous week   yr/yr growth</p>
<p>   Wheat	57.21 zl/q	 57.53 zl/q	 12.2 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  42.32 zl/q	 41.84 zl/q	 24.5 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     50.39 zl/q	 50.39 zl/q	 12.0 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal. --Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
